WEBVTT

00:00:07.708 --> 00:00:11.875
The second-term exams
culminated in our crushing victory.

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:15.333
But then our
disapproving principal showed up,

00:00:15.333 --> 00:00:18.042
and, hiding behind a notice
of Koro Sensei's dismissal,

00:00:18.042 --> 00:00:21.250
challenged our teacher to a one-sided wager.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:27.250
Now, Koro Sensei...
be a cornerstone of my philosophy.

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:32.625
"Training"

00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:42.583
"Training"

00:00:44.458 --> 00:00:48.125
Okay: opened, solved, and closed!

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.458
I more or less remember
which questions are on which page

00:00:51.458 --> 00:00:54.375
in this particular series of test books.

00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:56.417
Math was the only challenge.

00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:59.458
I'd lent that one out to a student
for so long that I'd forgotten.

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:00.667
Oh!

00:01:00.667 --> 00:01:03.500
You just <i>happened</i>
to have memorized the books

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:05.458
I just <i>happened </i>to bring?

00:01:05.458 --> 00:01:06.625
Heavens, no!

00:01:06.625 --> 00:01:10.375
I've memorized all of Japan's test books.

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:14.000
"No moving out of the blast radius
until you've solved the problem"?

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.167
A rule like that is no trouble
for a passionate educator.

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:22.125
Here I thought you understood me,

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:22.250
but it seems your students' defeat has unnerved you.

00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.458
"For Exams & Review!" "Exercise Problems" "Japanese"
but it seems your students' defeat has unnerved you.

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:32.250
You've dug your own grave
with this simplistic assassination.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:37.375
The last book... It's your turn.

00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.083
What's it feel like, having your own
death right before your eyes?

00:01:43.167 --> 00:01:47.667
That grand kaleidoscope glimpsed
in the moments before death...

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:53.542
What could be flashing through
that perfect mind of yours?

00:01:53.542 --> 00:01:54.583
Sir!

00:01:54.583 --> 00:01:55.958
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
Oh, sir!

00:01:55.958 --> 00:01:57.750
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
Mr. Asano!

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.000
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:15.167
<i>You're all I think about</i>

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:18.000
<i>Starting not to see anything else</i>

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.417
<i>I'll win your heart for sure--I swear</i>

00:02:23.417 --> 00:02:26.083
<i>Me, not cool? Oh, that old tale</i>

00:02:26.083 --> 00:02:28.792
<i>I've spared no effort since then</i>

00:02:28.792 --> 00:02:32.583
<i>Should be over my problems by now</i>

00:02:32.583 --> 00:02:36.625
<i>I'm brimming with confidence: I can do it</i>

00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:39.583
<i>And just when I get warmed up</i>

00:02:39.583 --> 00:02:44.792
<i>Yeah, I get knocked down like this every time</i>

00:02:44.792 --> 00:02:50.375
<i>Your scathing, serious voice cuts me</i>

00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:55.792
<i>Thousands, tens of thousands</i>
<i>of times I've given form to my feelings</i>

00:02:55.792 --> 00:03:01.292
<i>Driven them in,</i>
<i>thrown them in--but all you do is run</i>

00:03:01.292 --> 00:03:03.917
<i>Question, question: what</i>

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:06.583
<i>Question, question: on earth</i>

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:09.375
<i>Question, question: did I</i>

00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:11.958
<i>Ever know about you anyway?</i>

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:14.708
<i>Question, question: why</i>

00:03:14.708 --> 00:03:17.417
<i>Question, question: is it</i>

00:03:17.417 --> 00:03:20.250
<i>Question, question: you are</i>

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:25.208
<i>So close and yet so far away?</i>

00:03:28.958 --> 00:03:32.958
"13th Period: Let Live Time"
"by Yuzuki Fuwa"

00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:38.208
Two monsters took up teaching
at the same school:

00:03:38.208 --> 00:03:41.417
one to repent of his strength,

00:03:41.417 --> 00:03:44.917
one to repent of his weakness.

00:03:47.042 --> 00:03:50.750
Couldn't get me again today, Ikeda.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:55.042
A deal's a deal.
Be a good boy and study today.

00:03:55.042 --> 00:04:00.125
Dang! You're a real beast, Mr. Asano!

00:04:00.625 --> 00:04:02.542
Hey, Mr. Asano,

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.750
why'd you start a cram school
in this abandoned schoolhouse

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:06.250
up on this mountain, anyway?

00:04:06.250 --> 00:04:07.917
Didn't you graduate from a top school overseas

00:04:07.917 --> 00:04:09.958
with loads of credentials?

00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:13.000
Feels like a waste of talent and money to me.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.125
<i>And </i>a waste of energy making it up here.

00:04:15.125 --> 00:04:15.292
"Finding the Area of a Circle"
<i>And </i>a waste of energy making it up here.

00:04:15.292 --> 00:04:18.500
"Finding the Area of a Circle"
Nothing is for naught in this world of ours, Nagai.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:18.792
Nothing is for naught in this world of ours, Nagai.

00:04:18.792 --> 00:04:22.875
This mountain path is perfect
for training up your physical strength.

00:04:22.875 --> 00:04:23.625
Urk...

00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:26.583
And the money?
This place is in the red, isn't it?

00:04:26.583 --> 00:04:31.417
Don't worry, Mori.
My stocks will make up for the deficit.

00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:34.958
With my skill, they'll make money
even with minimal attention.

00:04:34.958 --> 00:04:37.417
This month, I'm about
500 thousand in the black.

00:04:37.417 --> 00:04:39.042
The perfect superhuman!

00:04:39.042 --> 00:04:42.542
You may be perfect,
but you're crazy into teaching.

00:04:42.542 --> 00:04:45.667
Just how do you intend
to educate us, anyway?

00:04:45.667 --> 00:04:50.167
Simple: Just grow into good students.

00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:53.417
But the bar for "good"
is different for everyone.

00:04:53.417 --> 00:04:56.375
Ikeda's high spirits are good.

00:04:56.375 --> 00:04:59.458
Mori's cleverness--<i>that's </i>good.

00:04:59.458 --> 00:05:01.750
And Nagai's diligence is good.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:05.042
But in order to make each
of your good points even better,

00:05:05.042 --> 00:05:09.333
As your teacher, I need to
get to know <i>all </i>of the "good" in you.

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:12.917
I'm only perfect because I have to be!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:14.292
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"

00:05:14.292 --> 00:05:17.417
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
The private cram school was off to a good start.

00:05:17.417 --> 00:05:21.000
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
Those three were the first students of my inaugural term.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:24.000
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
In the quiet of the mountain, I could cultivate their strengths

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.042
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
to my heart's content.

00:05:26.042 --> 00:05:28.792
The ideal education of my dreams...

00:05:31.208 --> 00:05:32.125
Ow!

00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:36.458
Hey, I gave you a heads-up!
Get outta the way, slowpoke!

00:05:36.458 --> 00:05:39.667
We're barely out of class,
and just look. You're so rowdy!

00:05:39.667 --> 00:05:42.500
I'm gonna be a basketball player!

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:45.167
--How could anyone just <i>study </i>all the time?
--Ow ow ow...

00:05:45.167 --> 00:05:47.833
A fine dream, Ikeda!

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:49.542
How about a little...

00:05:50.875 --> 00:05:52.667
...one-on-one?

00:05:52.667 --> 00:05:54.000
What do you say?

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:58.125
Ulp... Like I could win
against a perfect superhuman!

00:05:58.125 --> 00:06:03.833
Well, I <i>do </i>have abilities
you haven't yet been given...

00:06:03.833 --> 00:06:08.583
...just like not everyone
has the strengths you do.

00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:12.000
Sorry, Nagai.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:14.792
It's okay.

00:06:14.792 --> 00:06:16.958
Everyone has faults.

00:06:16.958 --> 00:06:18.750
I would tend to those faults,

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.583
cultivating people who could let their strengths

00:06:20.583 --> 00:06:23.708
shine to the fullest in society one day.

00:06:23.708 --> 00:06:27.208
I put everything I had into my lesson plans.

00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:28.667
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"

00:06:28.667 --> 00:06:34.167
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
The students were coming along well in just one short year.

00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:36.708
What's this?

00:06:36.708 --> 00:06:37.125
"Mission Accomplished!"
What's this?

00:06:37.125 --> 00:06:39.750
"Mission Accomplished!"
A <i>kunugi </i>oak-leaf tie clip!

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.125
"Mission Accomplished!"
We pooled our money together to buy it.

00:06:42.125 --> 00:06:45.292
"Mission Accomplished!"
It's probably peanuts compared to what you make on your stocks.

00:06:45.292 --> 00:06:48.500
"Mission Accomplished!"
Yep. I made another 7 million yesterday.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:51.833
"Mission Accomplished!"
He could've kept that to himself.

00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:55.083
But... this is lovely.

00:06:55.083 --> 00:06:57.458
We all got into our first-choice junior highs...

00:06:57.458 --> 00:06:59.750
We couldn't have done it
without you, Mr. Asano.

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:00.708
Yeah!

00:07:00.708 --> 00:07:04.375
When I grow up, I'll be a real good guy,
and I'll come see you!

00:07:06.708 --> 00:07:12.125
This is already enough.
You've grown into such good students.

00:07:12.208 --> 00:07:13.500
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:15.958
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
When they saw my résumé and my track record,

00:07:15.958 --> 00:07:19.625
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
more parents started entrusting their children to me.

00:07:19.625 --> 00:07:24.667
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
Three years later, the cram school was booming.

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:25.625
"Rikuto Ikeda"

00:07:25.625 --> 00:07:29.250
"Rikuto Ikeda"
Oh! What's it been, three years?

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:31.708
Good to hear from you, Ikeda!

00:07:31.708 --> 00:07:35.208
Long time no see, sir! Sounds like
you're at the top of your game!

00:07:35.208 --> 00:07:37.792
More or less. What's up?

00:07:37.792 --> 00:07:42.208
Oh, nothing really.
Just wondering how you were doing.

00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:44.375
Same as always.

00:07:44.375 --> 00:07:48.250
What about you? Not running wild
and causing trouble, I hope.

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:54.708
'Course not! I'm a solid hunk of caring,
just like you taught me!

00:07:54.708 --> 00:07:57.333
You sound busy. I'll call later.

00:07:57.333 --> 00:08:01.125
Maybe buy me a nice dinner
with your investment money, eh? Bye!

00:08:05.208 --> 00:08:09.083
I have an errand in his
neck of the woods next week.

00:08:09.083 --> 00:08:11.167
Maybe I'll stop by.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:20.333
"In Mourning"

00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:22.000
"In Mourning"
A suicide, they said.

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.500
There were some nasty older kids
on his squad, I heard.

00:08:25.500 --> 00:08:29.542
Beat him up, of course, but took
a fair amount of money off him, too.

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:33.500
He'd had a reputation as such a
sweet boy since junior high, too...

00:08:33.500 --> 00:08:35.458
Don't you think, you know...

00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:40.083
...he should have maybe
stood up for himself a little?

00:08:40.083 --> 00:08:43.542
What on earth had I been teaching?

00:08:43.542 --> 00:08:46.167
Cultivating good students?

00:08:46.167 --> 00:08:50.875
Dying in three years--
do you call <i>that </i>a good student?!

00:08:50.875 --> 00:08:57.167
If I don't build strong students...
this will all have been for nothing.

00:08:57.167 --> 00:09:02.208
But then what <i>is </i>"strong," anyway?

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.333
If I'm going to teach it,

00:09:04.333 --> 00:09:06.875
I'll need to get to know <i>all </i>of it.

00:09:08.125 --> 00:09:11.667
Things happened fast from there.

00:09:11.667 --> 00:09:14.875
I learned all there was
about all sorts of strengths.

00:09:14.875 --> 00:09:17.417
I sweet-talked the men who killed my student,

00:09:17.417 --> 00:09:21.833
leading them to become
ruined gambling addicts.

00:09:22.917 --> 00:09:27.958
I honed my brainwashing techniques on them.

00:09:27.958 --> 00:09:30.125
I opened another school.

00:09:30.125 --> 00:09:33.167
The campus that symbolized my weakness

00:09:33.167 --> 00:09:35.833
would serve as a lesson to the weak.

00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:41.833
Strong. I needed only to make them strong.

00:09:41.833 --> 00:09:44.583
Strong students who could survive,
if push came to shove,

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:47.750
even if it meant sacrificing others.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.083
And to that end...

00:09:51.083 --> 00:09:54.000
...I would need more money, more staff.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:57.542
If it could serve my education, I would use it.

00:09:57.542 --> 00:10:01.958
All to produce even one more of the strong.

00:10:03.792 --> 00:10:09.292
And now, both the weak
and the strong have left my side,

00:10:09.292 --> 00:10:13.833
and all I have before me is death.

00:10:13.833 --> 00:10:18.792
Well, Principal Asano?
Will you open the final book?

00:10:18.792 --> 00:10:22.417
No matter how superb you may be,
opening a grenade-filled test book

00:10:22.417 --> 00:10:24.250
will not end well.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.292
Hey, this was <i>your </i>wager.

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:30.167
If you don't wanna die,
just gracefully admit defeat!

00:10:30.167 --> 00:10:31.583
Yikes!

00:10:31.583 --> 00:10:36.250
And besides, we don't care
if you fire Koro Sensei!

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.917
It'll be sad to leave this place behind,

00:10:38.917 --> 00:10:41.875
but we'll go where Koro Sensei goes.

00:10:41.875 --> 00:10:46.167
Even if it means leaving home
or holing up in some mountain,

00:10:46.167 --> 00:10:50.625
we'll keep the assassination classroom
going till March.

00:10:50.625 --> 00:10:57.083
This year's E Class has been a constant
thorn in the side of my education...

00:10:57.083 --> 00:11:01.792
How many times now have I seen
such bald-faced opposition?

00:11:04.125 --> 00:11:06.375
Koro Sensei,

00:11:06.375 --> 00:11:08.750
under my educational philosophy,

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.875
you could very well destroy the earth

00:11:11.875 --> 00:11:15.125
and it wouldn't matter.

00:11:17.708 --> 00:11:23.625
Once the earth is gone,
the end will visit upon everyone equally.

00:11:23.625 --> 00:11:28.708
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
My students won't be the only ones suffering defeat.

00:11:28.708 --> 00:11:32.833
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"
That is one of my philosophy's ideals.

00:11:32.833 --> 00:11:34.875
"Kunugigaoka Cram School"

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:44.917
Have you forgotten my molt?

00:11:44.917 --> 00:11:47.875
Your once-monthly trick, eh?

00:11:47.875 --> 00:11:50.917
Why didn't you use it on yourself?

00:11:50.917 --> 00:11:53.292
I was saving it for you.

00:11:53.292 --> 00:11:59.625
If I'd won, there's no doubt
you'd have opted to blow yourself up.

00:11:59.625 --> 00:12:03.333
How can you be so sure what I'd do?

00:12:03.333 --> 00:12:06.333
Because we have so much in common.

00:12:06.333 --> 00:12:09.375
"Tentacle"
Both stubborn education fiends,

00:12:09.375 --> 00:12:14.083
aiming for perfection in teaching
even if it means using your own life.

00:12:14.083 --> 00:12:19.167
I talked to your old
cram-school students during the exams.

00:12:19.167 --> 00:12:22.833
About their impressions of you
as a teacher, about what happened...

00:12:22.833 --> 00:12:25.083
The educational ideals I pursue

00:12:25.083 --> 00:12:29.208
are identical to yours a dozen years back.

00:12:29.208 --> 00:12:34.833
Where I've been lucky,
compared to you, is with the E Class.

00:12:34.833 --> 00:12:37.125
Because there are a fair number of students

00:12:37.125 --> 00:12:39.458
and because they share
the same circumstances,

00:12:39.458 --> 00:12:42.250
they came together to withstand training

00:12:42.250 --> 00:12:45.917
and can ask each other for advice
without holding things in.

00:12:45.917 --> 00:12:53.750
And, Principal Asano, it's none other
than <i>you </i>who made this E Class.

00:12:53.750 --> 00:12:57.500
You've unconsciously been
carrying on the ideal education

00:12:57.500 --> 00:13:00.417
you came up with long ago.

00:13:00.417 --> 00:13:03.542
I'm the only one this knife can kill.

00:13:03.542 --> 00:13:06.958
We do not teach the theft of human life.

00:13:06.958 --> 00:13:10.167
You and I share the same ideals:

00:13:10.167 --> 00:13:13.417
not a killing education, but one that lets live.

00:13:13.417 --> 00:13:18.750
Let's keep on following through
with our ideal education.

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:22.875
Playing outside is fine,
but not playing hooky, Ikeda.

00:13:22.875 --> 00:13:26.542
Hmph! Kids are all about
bein' active, not studyin'!

00:13:26.542 --> 00:13:29.958
Hmm. Well, how about this?

00:13:29.958 --> 00:13:34.458
You can attack me once a day,
whenever you like.

00:13:34.458 --> 00:13:37.542
If you can hit me,
I'll let you skip class that day.

00:13:37.542 --> 00:13:40.167
Seriously? Promise?

00:13:40.167 --> 00:13:41.458
Yep.

00:13:41.458 --> 00:13:44.083
You gotta see it through
to the end, Mr. Asano!

00:13:44.083 --> 00:13:46.875
No runnin' off halfway!

00:13:48.750 --> 00:13:51.708
My philosophy is always correct.

00:13:51.708 --> 00:13:56.667
I've turned out a great number of
strong students these past dozen years.

00:13:56.667 --> 00:14:01.542
But now you've acknowledged
my system as well,

00:14:01.542 --> 00:14:06.292
so I will deign to
permit this E Class to remain.

00:14:07.875 --> 00:14:11.667
Still can't simply admit defeat, I see.

00:14:11.667 --> 00:14:13.542
Oh, and...

00:14:13.542 --> 00:14:17.000
May I come by and kill you now and then?

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.708
Of course.

00:14:18.708 --> 00:14:21.708
That knife suits a worthy rival well.

00:14:27.625 --> 00:14:30.042
The perfect façade is crumbling...

00:14:30.042 --> 00:14:33.542
I can tell by your face
you've lost again, Father.

00:14:33.542 --> 00:14:36.042
Did you need something, Asano?

00:14:36.042 --> 00:14:39.250
Just thought I'd come
cheer up my loser father

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:41.542
by asking for compensation for this

00:14:41.542 --> 00:14:45.833
along with a grade-A prime Kobe steak.

00:14:45.833 --> 00:14:47.333
Aha...

00:14:47.333 --> 00:14:51.500
Take me to court on
domestic violence charges if you like.

00:14:51.500 --> 00:14:56.167
You'll never win against me,
no matter how much you grow.

00:14:56.167 --> 00:14:58.417
What makes you say that?

00:14:58.417 --> 00:15:02.958
Because I'll keep growing, too. As an educator

00:15:02.958 --> 00:15:05.167
and as a parent.

00:15:06.417 --> 00:15:07.792
By the way, sir...

00:15:07.792 --> 00:15:10.583
Where's our reward for the exams?

00:15:10.583 --> 00:15:12.083
Oh, right!

00:15:12.083 --> 00:15:16.625
I promised to tell you
my crucial weakness, didn't I?

00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:19.875
In fact, I have surprisingly little power.

00:15:19.875 --> 00:15:21.250
"Can be captured if everyone holds him down"
In fact, I have surprisingly little power.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.750
"Can be captured if everyone holds him down"
I'm too specialized for speed.

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:23.333
I'm too specialized for speed.

00:15:23.333 --> 00:15:25.917
When I'm at a standstill, even a single human

00:15:25.917 --> 00:15:28.667
can hold back one of my tentacles.

00:15:28.667 --> 00:15:32.250
So if we all locked down
all of your tentacles...

00:15:32.250 --> 00:15:36.000
...we could stop you from moving?

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.042
If we could do <i>that</i>,
this woulda been a cakewalk!

00:15:39.042 --> 00:15:41.917
You only told us 'cause you knew
it was impossible, octopus!

00:15:41.917 --> 00:15:43.833
Hmm. No luck, eh?

00:15:43.833 --> 00:15:44.083
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season" "by Karma Akabane"
Hmm. No luck, eh?

00:15:44.083 --> 00:15:47.875
"Assassination Classroom, Second Season" "by Karma Akabane"
The trick is to pretend you're grabbing a slime eel.

00:15:49.375 --> 00:15:51.833
A drama festival?!

00:15:51.833 --> 00:15:54.417
"Drama Festival!"
Now, when we're about to take high-school entrance exams?

00:15:54.417 --> 00:15:58.167
"Drama Festival!"
I complained to Asano about it at the student council meeting,

00:15:58.167 --> 00:16:00.625
but he shot back,

00:16:00.625 --> 00:16:05.292
It's training to memorize lines and
stage directions in a short period of time.

00:16:05.292 --> 00:16:08.917
All part of Kunugigaoka
Junior High educational policies.

00:16:08.917 --> 00:16:09.833
Besides, it's <i>you </i>guys. You'll figure it out.

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:12.792
"Budgeting" "After performances, return to classrooms"
Besides, it's <i>you </i>guys. You'll figure it out.

00:16:13.208 --> 00:16:14.958
Nice.

00:16:14.958 --> 00:16:16.875
Nagisa! Nagisa!

00:16:16.875 --> 00:16:19.042
"Sada Abe: This is Mine"
<i>You </i>play the lead!

00:16:19.042 --> 00:16:21.958
"Sada Abe: This is Mine"
Not another dodgy suggestion...

00:16:21.958 --> 00:16:23.958
What about you, Kayano?

00:16:23.958 --> 00:16:28.083
The kids were really into
your play at the preschool.

00:16:28.083 --> 00:16:31.833
--Huh? But I--
--Like that'll work with a junior-high audience!

00:16:31.833 --> 00:16:35.167
They ain't gonna see themselves
in some pint-sized player!

00:16:35.167 --> 00:16:36.625
Hah!

00:16:36.625 --> 00:16:40.000
I'd like to work on props.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.667
Okay, so for our main staff,

00:16:42.667 --> 00:16:44.375
we have Mimura the director,

00:16:44.375 --> 00:16:46.917
and Hazama'd make a good writer.

00:16:46.917 --> 00:16:48.583
As for our leads...

00:16:48.583 --> 00:16:50.083
--I want to play the lead.

00:16:50.083 --> 00:16:52.417
--Yeah, right! You, a state secret?
--I want to play the lead.

00:16:52.417 --> 00:16:55.083
We can't be putting a huge
grown-up on stage anyway!

00:16:55.083 --> 00:16:58.708
B-But I've always wanted
to be the lead in a play!

00:16:58.708 --> 00:17:01.458
And I want to stand on
the same stage with you all!

00:17:01.458 --> 00:17:03.917
Sure. I've got just the thing.

00:17:03.917 --> 00:17:08.125
A play that'll satisfy the wishes
of both assassins and target!

00:17:08.625 --> 00:17:10.333
Okay, here's our chance!

00:17:10.333 --> 00:17:14.458
Let's whip those main-campus mooks
into a storm of excitement!

00:17:16.792 --> 00:17:18.125
Let's see...

00:17:18.125 --> 00:17:19.625
Next up is the E Class.

00:17:19.625 --> 00:17:23.417
Let's just sneer at 'em while we eat.

00:17:26.042 --> 00:17:27.708
A peach.

00:17:31.250 --> 00:17:34.458
According to the sonogram,

00:17:34.458 --> 00:17:38.750
there's a baby growing inside.

00:17:38.750 --> 00:17:41.792
The old man's eyes lit up

00:17:41.792 --> 00:17:45.458
as he instantly realized
the value of this peach.

00:17:45.458 --> 00:17:50.500
How marvelous! A rarity, indeed!
The media'll be all over this one!

00:17:50.500 --> 00:17:53.958
If I put this on display,
I'll be rich for the rest of my life!

00:17:53.958 --> 00:17:55.625
Eh?

00:17:55.625 --> 00:17:57.417
Divorce papers.

00:17:57.417 --> 00:18:00.958
The old woman had been
wavering over whether to leave him.

00:18:00.958 --> 00:18:03.833
But the old man's disregard
for children's rights

00:18:03.833 --> 00:18:05.875
along with his cruel words--

00:18:05.875 --> 00:18:06.375
"Script"
along with his cruel words--

00:18:06.375 --> 00:18:09.625
"Script"
"I" and "my," not "we" and "our"--

00:18:09.625 --> 00:18:10.125
"I" and "my," not "we" and "our"--

00:18:10.125 --> 00:18:14.417
made up her mind at last.

00:18:14.417 --> 00:18:18.875
The furrow that had formed between them
over thirty years of marriage

00:18:18.875 --> 00:18:22.958
was like the river where she did the washing.

00:18:22.958 --> 00:18:27.542
The stifling air between them
was like the carbon dioxide

00:18:27.542 --> 00:18:29.750
from burning mountain firewood.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:32.375
This peach is all mine.

00:18:32.375 --> 00:18:35.208
I'm the head of the household--

00:18:35.208 --> 00:18:37.833
I decide how to divide our shared property!

00:18:39.375 --> 00:18:41.167
Lawyers.

00:18:41.167 --> 00:18:46.625
We represent your wife. Any further
communication must go through us.

00:18:46.625 --> 00:18:51.375
About the peach...
As your marriage had failed long ago,

00:18:51.375 --> 00:18:55.292
the cut-off date for
dividing your assets is long past.

00:18:55.292 --> 00:18:57.125
Add in reparations for emotional harassment,

00:18:57.125 --> 00:19:00.292
and one peach isn't going to cut it.

00:19:00.292 --> 00:19:04.500
Thirty years of harsh words
and actions directed at the old lady.

00:19:04.500 --> 00:19:08.042
"Diary" "Bank Book"
He'd stopped bringing in a living wage a while back.

00:19:08.042 --> 00:19:10.500
"Diary" "Bank Book"
She had plenty of evidence.

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:13.500
"Diary" "Bank Book"
The old man had no hope of winning in court.

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:14.542
"Illegal Drugs"
The old man had no hope of winning in court.

00:19:14.542 --> 00:19:16.292
"Illegal Drugs"
The local men he'd hired to intimidate her

00:19:16.292 --> 00:19:17.417
The local men he'd hired to intimidate her

00:19:17.417 --> 00:19:20.333
were hauled off by the police.

00:19:21.583 --> 00:19:25.667
The old lady brought the peach
to her new home.

00:19:25.667 --> 00:19:29.750
She felt bright and cheerful,
like her life had been laundered.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:31.167
--Her new life with the peach had begun.

00:19:31.167 --> 00:19:36.000
--One, two, one, two... hooray!
--Her new life with the peach had begun.

00:19:42.625 --> 00:19:45.042
A dog, a monkey, a pheasant.

00:19:45.042 --> 00:19:48.500
It seems they're being trained to attack people.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:54.167
The wild animals ate their food
and innocently followed orders.

00:19:54.167 --> 00:19:59.333
The only evil one was the old man,
tainted by his lust for wealth.

00:19:59.333 --> 00:20:05.583
Perhaps the demon island
Onigashima is inside us after all...

00:20:05.583 --> 00:20:09.583
The peach child will be born soon.

00:20:09.583 --> 00:20:12.292
Will he, too, host a demon one day?

00:20:17.875 --> 00:20:19.750
Th--

00:20:19.750 --> 00:20:20.667
That's <i>heavy</i>!

00:20:20.667 --> 00:20:23.417
It totally ruined my appetite!

00:20:24.875 --> 00:20:29.667
Funny how words can leave marks.

00:20:29.667 --> 00:20:32.708
I'm the lead! The lead!

00:20:32.708 --> 00:20:35.333
That blasted E Class!

00:20:36.458 --> 00:20:42.833
My school has wound up
right in this creature's tentacles.

00:20:42.833 --> 00:20:48.875
But the E Class won't end
quite so happily ever after.

00:20:48.875 --> 00:20:51.792
With what I've heard
from the Ministry of Defense

00:20:51.792 --> 00:20:56.292
and from my own experience here...

00:20:56.292 --> 00:21:01.208
I'm the only one who can
predict what will happen next.

00:21:01.208 --> 00:21:02.500
--Come on!
--Can you still be a teacher...

00:21:02.500 --> 00:21:04.208
--Hurry up already!
--Can you still be a teacher...

00:21:04.208 --> 00:21:07.875
...in the wake of the biggest storm ever?

00:21:20.375 --> 00:21:25.875
<i>The moon that swims in the night sky</i>

00:21:25.875 --> 00:21:31.250
<i>If you stretch out your hand, you can reach it</i>

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:36.917
<i>I went to touch it: it was warm</i>

00:21:36.917 --> 00:21:42.042
<i>And slowly drew me in</i>

00:21:42.042 --> 00:21:53.417
<i>The multiplying footsteps,</i>
<i>the view from my window:</i>

00:21:53.417 --> 00:21:59.000
<i>As I drifted along, expressionless</i>

00:21:59.000 --> 00:22:03.458
<i>They spilled out of my hands</i>

00:22:03.458 --> 00:22:10.292
<i>It was rocking, swaying--I never knew</i>

00:22:10.292 --> 00:22:15.792
<i>Until I touched it with my own hands</i>

00:22:15.792 --> 00:22:21.250
<i>I'll gather up</i>
<i>and go through all of the things</i>

00:22:21.250 --> 00:22:28.583
<i>Scattered beneath the waning moon</i>

00:22:40.167 --> 00:22:41.292
Surprise!

00:22:41.292 --> 00:22:41.333
Not-Needed Kunudon!

00:22:41.333 --> 00:22:41.958
"Tell Us, Kunudon!"
Not-Needed Kunudon!

00:22:41.958 --> 00:22:44.000
"Not-Needed Kunudon!"
Not-Needed Kunudon!

00:22:44.500 --> 00:22:45.333
"Sake for Good Boys & Girls"

00:22:45.333 --> 00:22:49.042
With the school infighting over,
he had served his purpose

00:22:49.042 --> 00:22:51.875
and was sent to the E Class.

00:22:51.875 --> 00:22:54.583
Get away from me, y'riffraff!

00:22:54.583 --> 00:22:56.917
I ain't like the rest o' you!

00:22:56.917 --> 00:22:57.208
Three cheers for unemployment!

00:22:57.208 --> 00:22:58.958
"Goodbye, Kunudon! (Societally Speaking)"
Three cheers for unemployment!

00:22:58.958 --> 00:23:02.016
"Goodbye, Kunudon! (Societally Speaking)"
Goodbye, Kunudon!
